# <%= current_page.data.title %>

[cnp-jenkins-library](https://github.com/hmcts/cnp-jenkins-library) — the
library behind the common pipeline — is released as semantic version tags
(for example `2.7.1`). The available versions are listed on the
[library tags page](https://github.com/hmcts/cnp-jenkins-library/tags).

## Consume a pinned version

Pin the library to a release in your `Jenkinsfile_CNP` (and `Jenkinsfile_nightly`):

```groovy
@Library("Infrastructure@2.7.1") _
```

Pinning to a released version is the default mechanism. A bare
`@Library("Infrastructure")` follows a branch and picks up every change as
soon as it merges — avoid it, so your pipeline only changes when you update
the pin.

See the [Jenkins library guide](/cloud-native-platform/shared-libraries/jenkins-library.html)
for how to import and use the library itself.

## Upgrade path

You do not need to watch for new releases yourself. The
[HMCTS global Renovate configuration](renovate.html) contains a custom manager
that finds `@Library("Infrastructure@<version>")` pins in any `Jenkinsfile_*`
file and tracks them against the library's GitHub tags:

- **Minor and patch updates** are raised as pull requests and **automerge**
  once your CI checks pass.
- **Major updates** are raised as pull requests but are **never automerged** —
  a major version signals a breaking change, so review the release notes
  and test before merging.

If your repository is not yet onboarded to Renovate, update the pin manually
by editing the version in your Jenkinsfiles and letting the pull request
build verify it.

## Testing an unmerged library change

To test a library branch before it is released, reference the branch:

```groovy
@Library("Infrastructure@my-feature-branch") _
```

Branches must first be added to the
[allowed library branches list](https://github.com/hmcts/cnp-jenkins-library/blob/master/resources/uk/gov/hmcts/library/allowed-library-branches.yml)
and that change merged, otherwise the pipeline will fail. Switch back to a
pinned release once the change has been released.
